---
// Resume page: a web summary of the resume plus the PDF download.
// To change the wording, edit the text between the tags below.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/urls';
---
<Base title="Resume | Brewster Smyers">
  <section class="page-heading wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Experience + education</p>
    <h1>Brewster Smyers<span>.</span></h1>
    <p>Mechanical engineering student · Bucknell University · Expected May 2028</p>
    <a class="button" href={url('resume/Brewster_Smyers_Resume.pdf')} download>Download resume PDF <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
  </section>

  <section class="resume-layout wrap">
    {/* Left column: quick facts */}
    <aside>
      <p class="eyebrow">At a glance</p>
      <p>B.S. Mechanical Engineering</p>
      <p>Minors in Mathematics and Business Analytics</p>
      <p>Marblehead, Massachusetts</p>
      <a class="text-link" href={url('contact/')}>Contact ↗</a>
    </aside>

    {/* Right column: the resume itself */}
    <article class="prose">
      <h2>Technical foundation</h2>
      <p>SolidWorks (CSWA), FEA simulation, Mastercam, MATLAB, Python, Java, carpentry and Microsoft Office.</p>

      <h2>Selected engineering work</h2>
      <h3><a href={url('projects/outdoor-landmark-chair/')}>Outdoor Landmark Chair</a></h3>
      <p>Independent design and fabrication. Designed a braced-frame outdoor chair in SolidWorks with a preliminary stress study, then built it alone in two days on a budget of about $1,000. It seats four to five people and is still in use.</p>
      <h3><a href={url('projects/ack-coaster-mold/')}>Nantucket Coaster Injection Mold</a></h3>
      <p>Manufacturing Processes, Fall 2026. Designed a coaster and its aluminum injection mold, then wrote the process plan and Mastercam toolpaths (5 tools, 880 lines of G-code). The mold was machined on a Haas mill from my G-code.</p>
      <h3><a href={url('projects/bronze-cast-rook/')}>Bronze Cast Rook</a></h3>
      <p>Manufacturing Processes, Fall 2026. Designed and 3D printed a pattern, built the wax gating and cast it in bronze. Measured against CAD, the width came out 3.36% smaller and the mass about 14% below prediction.</p>
      <h3><a href={url('projects/pipe-brace-bracket/')}>90° Pipe Brace Bracket</a></h3>
      <p>Independent FEA study, November 2026. Ran a static FEA at 1,000 N in SolidWorks Simulation, confirmed the 140 MPa bend stress by hand and traced a 376 MPa peak to a sharp corner in the model.</p>
      <h3><a href={url('projects/autonomous-underwater-vehicle/')}>Underwater Vehicle and Water Tunnel</a></h3>
      <p>Team lead, Fluid Dynamics project, Fall 2026, in progress. Leading a team of six that is designing an underwater vehicle hull and a miniature water tunnel to test a scale model. I own the tunnel design and did the hull hydrostatics and buoyancy calculations by hand.</p>
      <h3><a href={url('projects/aerobatic-biplane/')}>Aerobatic Biplane</a></h3>
      <p>SolidWorks and MATLAB concept study, Fall 2026. Modeled a two-seat biplane and adapted a MATLAB analysis of lift, drag, fuel use, power and trim.</p>

      <h2>Leadership + service</h2>
      <h3>Infrastructure and Social Chair · Sigma Phi Epsilon</h3>
      <p>Designed and constructed modular risers, seating and stages, and coordinated event logistics, vendors and member participation.</p>
      <h3>Teaching and Mentoring Assistant · LEAP for Education</h3>
      <p>Summers 2022 and 2023. Supported students through seasonal educational outreach and mentoring.</p>

      <h2>Work experience</h2>
      <h3>Bartender · The Nantucket Hotel & Resort</h3>
      <p>2026. High-volume service across the bar, pool, guest rooms and restaurant, including weddings and special events.</p>
      <h3>Bartender · The Landing</h3>
      <p>2022–2025 · Marblehead, Massachusetts. Coordinated bar service, food and drink orders, preparation and restaurant support.</p>

      <p class="muted">The PDF is the full one-page résumé.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
</Base>
